MAJOR_VERSION=5
STANDARD_VERSION=4
RELEASE_VERSION=0
PRERELEASE=1
DEV_VERSION=1
DESCRIPTION=KeyQuorum account keys, signed bridges, bridges in server file sharing, and canonical account names in the freestanding kernel and browser lab. Every account now has its own KeyQuorum Ed25519 signing key, sealed under the account's password (KeyQuorum KQAK: Argon2id and AES-256-GCM) in new signing_public and signing_sealed columns of the account store, added in place: useradd creates it, userdel deletes it with the account, an account from before keys gets one at its next login, passwd for yourself asks for the current password and keeps the key, and a reset by an ancestor gives the account a new key. Bridges are signed: bridge request and bridge accept ask for the password and sign with that key over the two key ids, the signer and a random nonce (KeyQuorum signing::account_bridge_preimage, KQ-ACCOUNT-BRIDGE-v1); the bridges table gains nonce, request_sig and accept_sig, and a bridge counts only while both signatures verify under the signers' current keys, so unsigned, changed or re-keyed bridges open nothing and bridge list shows them as unsigned. server file -user now runs a sender-side gate (kernel/core/identity/share_gate.c): the receiver must be an account with a key, on the sender's own line, or joined by a signed active bridge, or the offer is refused with the reason. The freestanding kernel and browser lab use the canonical Flinstone and Root spellings, matched regardless of case. The KeyQuorum submodule moves to the commit that adds the account key C ABI (ffi/identity kq_account_*). Tests: test_heritage covers keys, signed and tampered bridges, key keeping and replacement, and the share gate; the lab and freestanding shell expectations use the canonical names.

RELEASE_DATE=2026-10-20
